  "prototypeNotes": [
    "Acknowledging a warning does not make an invalid Character valid.",
    "Acknowledgements never resolve invalidations and never bypass blocking or error rules.",
    "Only the user may accept a warning; the Narrator and Chronicle Director cannot do so.",
    "Reusability depends on the warning scope, fingerprint, declared dependencies, Character version, and package binding.",
    "Completion-attempt acknowledgements expire after the exact attempt or when the draft version changes.",
    "Chronicle owns identity, persistence, encryption, fingerprints, expiration state, and events.",
    "The Rule Set owns warning definitions, acknowledgement requirements, scopes, and matching rules."
  ]
